// the whole box (position plus the labels' shape, zeros included) inside
// the dataset.  An item that is not one is refused at the PUSH -- the whole
// `OverlayUpdate` is not applied and the plugin is told which rule, on
// `ContractViolation.where = VIOLATION_SITE_OVERLAY_ITEM_REFUSED` -- and
// refused again by CompileLabelVolume with a `host_error`, which cannot rely
// on the push having been checked (§5.3: a request drains ahead of the push
// it repeats).  The box can only be checked while a dataset is open; a push
// with none open is applied unchecked and the compile refuses it NOT_FOUND.
// Display and compile therefore agree on what the item is; the one thing
// that displays and does NOT compile is inline geometry, which is the
// compile's TRANSPORT rule (no voxel bytes on the control plane), not part
// of the definition -- send it segment-backed if it will be committed.
//
