// only; a foreground label `id` (>= 1) is drawn with row `1 + (id - 1) mod
// 255`, so ids 1..255 use rows 1..255 directly and ids above 255 wrap onto
// the foreground rows with period 255 — NEVER onto row 0.  (An earlier rule,
// `id mod 256`, put label 256 on the background row: invisible in both views
// and compiled with `visible = false`.)  Row 0's alpha is the
// background's, conventionally 0.  A row's alpha is the ROW's -- it is shared
// by every id that maps to it -- and the compile (§8.8) persists it as the
// region's `visible` unless `label_visible` names that id.  It was documented
