// NEITHER is bound, and the host tells the user which plugins collided and on
// what.  Not first-come, not last-wins, not a silent re-map -- a user has to be
// able to know what their keys do, and a binding that silently went to one of
// two plugins is exactly what they cannot find out.  The recourse is theirs:
// stop both, start the one whose binding they want.
//
// NO field carries a platform code, by the rule `doorbell_E_input.md` §3
