// so level-N pixel j covers level-0 [j*s, j*s+s-1] and is CENTERED at
// j*s + (s-1)/2, not at j*s; the +-0.5 is that grid phase.  Dropping it shifts
// every bound by 0.5*(s-1)/s level-N pixels and fails inward at the low face,
// silently omitting a plane that is inside the crop.  A level-0 INDEX has no
